   "source": [
    "The dataset is moderately clean but contains missing values in key columns.\n",
    "The size column has missing categorical values which can be filled with “Unknown” to preserve product information.\n",
    "The customer_rating column contains missing numerical values likely due to unrated or new products, and these can be imputed using the mean rating to maintain statistical consistency.\n",
    "The return_reason column has a high number of missing values, which likely indicates non-returned items; therefore, missing values can be replaced with “Not Returned” to preserve business meaning.\n",
    "Overall, the dataset is usable after handling missing values appropriately based on data type and context."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "b60f2bc2-a7fa-4763-afd5-ad431c59a081",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df['size'] = df['size'].fillna(\"Unknown\")\n",
    "df['customer_rating'] = df['customer_rating'].fillna(df['customer_rating'].mean())\n",
    "df['return_reason'] = df['return_reason'].fillna(\"Not Returned\")"
   ]
  },
